=== SURVEY ===
Web source Breadcrumbs.tsx is the pure, presentational breadcrumb trail. Props: `items: BreadcrumbItem[]`
(`{ label, href? }`), `homeHref = '/'`, `homeAriaLabel`. Behaviour (verbatim):
  • `if (items.length <= 1) return null;` — a top-level page renders no breadcrumb (self-suppression).
  • `<nav aria-label={t('a11y.breadcrumb','Breadcrumb')}>` wraps a leading Home link
    (`<PrefetchLink to={homeHref}>` around the `Home` glyph, aria `homeAriaLabel ??
    t('a11y.breadcrumbHome','Dashboard')`), then `items.map`: a `<ChevronRight>` + per item either a
    `<span>` (when `isLast || !item.href`) or a `<PrefetchLink to={item.href}>`; the trailing item is
    `text-secondary font-medium`, the rest `text-muted`; every crumb `truncate max-w-[200px]`.
  • Middle items (`i>0 && !isLast`) are `hidden sm:inline` with a `…` (`aria-hidden`) on a narrow screen.
Only hook: `useTranslation` (the file imports Fragment, PrefetchLink, lucide icons, cn — NO data hook).
i18n keys extracted: `a11y.breadcrumb` → "Breadcrumb"; `a11y.breadcrumbHome` → "Dashboard".
Shared components from source: none. Charts/maps: none.
Existing native: NO `Breadcrumbs`/`BreadcrumbsItem`/`BreadcrumbsModel`/`BreadcrumbsSurface`/
`BreadcrumbsTrailView`/`BreadcrumbsProjection` symbols (grep = 0; the sibling ports `LayoutBreadcrumbs.*`
(0170) + `BreadcrumbOverridesContext.*` (0166) use their own prefixes — no collision). Canonical
predecessors studied: BreadcrumbOverridesContext (0166, the trail renderer for the wired variant) +
LayoutBreadcrumbs (0170) — repo convention is per-surface self-contained types; both documented the
"no loading/error/stale/offline (reads no remote data)" disposition + the horizontal-scroll overflow
adaptation. This prompt (0167) owns a STANDALONE port of the pure component into its own allowed files.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is pure + presentational; the prompt requires a production-polished native surface
  reproducing its DATA, composition, states and i18n, with every state visible (no blank box). Chosen
  architecture mirrors the canonical per-surface split, all types prefixed `Breadcrumbs` (self-contained,
  no coupling to the sibling ports — the allowed-files set is Breadcrumbs.* only):
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): BreadcrumbsSurface.slug; BreadcrumbsItem (web BreadcrumbItem);
    BreadcrumbsCrumb (a rendered crumb: .item(label,href,isCurrent) | .ellipsis, Identifiable);
    BreadcrumbsResolved (suppression/render/empty/collapsed/current read-model); BreadcrumbsProjection
    (suppression `<= 1 → []`, current-leaf href-drop, compact middle→single-ellipsis collapse).
  • Model: BreadcrumbsStrings i18n facade (a11y.breadcrumb / a11y.breadcrumbHome verbatim keys +
    English fallbacks); BreadcrumbsTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; @Observable
    @MainActor BreadcrumbsModel (holds items + Home a11y override, re-projects on update, emits
    view.opened once, idempotent across stop/start).
  • Surface (Breadcrumbs.swift): the public View — model + items inits, navigation callbacks
    (onHome / onSelect, the Apple peer of <PrefetchLink to>), size-class-aware projection, renders
    the trail or the empty slot, onAppear start / onDisappear stop.
  • Views: BreadcrumbsTrailView (horizontal-scroll <nav> body: Home button, chevrons, link-vs-text
    crumbs, current-leaf emphasis, 200pt truncation, ellipsis), BreadcrumbsEmptySlot (web `null` peer),
    DEBUG inspector (every scenario rendered — never a blank box). Previews + strings + Tests/AdapterTests.
- States rendered (exactly the source's branches — covenant #3 no skip-and-assume, #5 no parity
  shortcuts): rendered (multi-item trail, regular width); collapsed (compact width → first · ellipsis ·
  current leaf, the web `hidden sm:inline` + `…`); suppressed (single item, web `items.length <= 1 →
  null`); empty (no items). loading/error/stale/offline DO NOT EXIST in the source (its only hook is
  useTranslation; items are props) — inventing freshness chrome would be drift, so the DEBUG inspector
  renders a friendly note for the two non-drawing branches instead of a blank box. This is the
  predecessor-accepted disposition for this anonymous/props-only component family (0166/0170).
- Native adaptation (documented, not a shortcut): the web hides middle items behind an ellipsis on a
  narrow screen; the idiomatic Apple peer is a single collapsed `…` between the first crumb and the
  current leaf on a compact horizontal size class (computed by the pure projection), inside a horizontal
  ScrollView so an overflowing chain on any width stays fully reachable. Data, order, links, current-leaf
  emphasis, 200pt truncation and suppression are reproduced exactly. There is no motion to gate for
  Reduce Motion (the web only animates a CSS hover colour, which has no native peer).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind classes literally (used P1/S9 tokens); reusing the sibling
  BreadcrumbOverridesTrailView (allowed files are Breadcrumbs.* only → self-contained types);
  one `…` per hidden middle item (a single collapsed indicator is the idiomatic Apple treatment);
  hrefs on the view boundary (navigation surfaced as callbacks — the Apple peer of <PrefetchLink to>).

